WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.825
Now for the trap.

2
00:00:02.075 --> 00:00:10.125
Rule eighteen opens with six words that the exam loves: except where Rules nine, ten and thirteen otherwise require.

3
00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:12.825
So the ladder has three exceptions.

4
00:00:13.075 --> 00:00:15.425
Rule nine, narrow channels.

5
00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:23.175
A sailing vessel, or any vessel under twenty meters, shall not impede a vessel that can navigate only within the channel.

6
00:00:23.425 --> 00:00:26.500
Rule ten, traffic separation schemes.

7
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.900
The same idea applies to vessels following a traffic lane.

8
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.750
And Rule thirteen, overtaking.

9
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.975
The overtaking vessel always keeps clear, whatever she is.

10
00:00:38.225 --> 00:00:40.000
So try this one.

11
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:46.025
A sailboat is tacking up the ship channel in Tampa Bay, and a loaded tanker is coming down it.

12
00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:49.275
On the ladder, sail stands above power.

13
00:00:49.525 --> 00:00:51.725
Who has to stay out of the way?

14
00:00:52.725 --> 00:00:54.325
The sailboat.

15
00:00:54.575 --> 00:00:59.250
She must not impede the tanker, because Rule nine overrides the ladder.

16
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.550
Here’s your exam habit.

17
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:09.000
Before you apply the ladder, check the question for three things: a narrow channel, a traffic lane, or overtaking.
